* For the anti projectile properties, all versions have to be timed with the projectile
----
B Version
*Combos from lights
*Frame traps from lights
*Gives small combo on counter hit
*Nullify projectiles

A safe true string block ender from heavies and the go to frame trap from lights. Due to long active frames, can easily setup up meaty stomps that can be up to +4 on block and +8 on hit. It is your go to to nullify projectiles on reaction.
----
D Version
*Most optimal DP punish starter 
*Frame traps and combos from cl.C
*Nullify projectiles
*On hit, can link into 2C
Mainly used as damaging combo filler and his most damaging punish starter on DP reversals. It is pretty slow to nullify projectiles so it can only be used from full screen.
----
BD Version
*First hit can break to be +4 
*True strings into Groove stance 50/50 or Amazing Run strike throw situation
*Can reflect projectiles 
*True strings from heavies
Salvatore's most important pressure tool and combo extender. On hit it leads to all his optimal Rev combos. On block it gets his offense going even when not cancelled into anything. Break is the preferred pressure choice due to the strength of being able to catch mashing and jumps/backdash with 2C. However letting it rip is also good to setup all the potential mixup scenarios and be +2 but right up the opponent's face. It is his strongest tool against ex fireballs being able to stop most of opponents attempts to skip neutral moving behind them.
}}

